Here is a standard Declarative Jenkinsfile template. It includes the most common pipeline stages (Checkout, Build, Test, Deploy) along with environment variables and post-build actions.

```groovy
pipeline {
    // Execute the pipeline on any available Jenkins agent
    agent any 

    // Define global environment variables
    environment {
        APP_NAME = 'my-application'
        BUILD_ENV = 'production'
    }

    // Pipeline stages
    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                echo 'Checking out source code...'
                // Automatically checks out code from the repository this Jenkinsfile is in
                checkout scm 
            }
        }

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                echo "Building ${APP_NAME}..."
                // Replace with your project's build command
                // e.g., sh 'npm install && npm run build' (Node.js) 
                // or sh 'mvn clean package' (Java/Maven)
                sh 'make build' 
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                echo 'Running tests...'
                // Replace with your project's test command
                sh 'make test' 
            }
            post {
                always {
                    // Example of archiving test reports
                    // junit '**/target/surefire-reports/TEST-*.xml'
                    echo 'Processing test results...'
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy') {
            // Conditional execution: only run this stage if on the main branch
            when {
                branch 'main' 
            }
            steps {
                echo 'Deploying application...'
                // Add your deployment scripts/commands here
                sh 'make deploy'
            }
        }
    }

    // Actions to run at the end of the pipeline based on the status
    post {
        success {
            echo '✅ Pipeline completed successfully!'
            // Add notification logic here (e.g., Slack, Email)
        }
        failure {
            echo '❌ Pipeline failed. Please check the logs.'
        }
        always {
            echo '🧹 Cleaning up workspace...'
            // Cleans the workspace to free up disk space and prevent dirty builds
            cleanWs() 
        }
    }
}
```

### How to customize this template:
* **`agent`**: You can restrict this to specific build nodes using labels (e.g., `agent { label 'linux' }`) or run it inside a Docker container (`agent { docker { image 'node:18-alpine' } }`).
* **`sh` steps**: Replace the `make ...` placeholder shell commands with the actual commands needed for your tech stack (like `npm`, `yarn`, `mvn`, `gradle`, or `go`).
* **`when` block**: The deploy stage is currently configured to only run when changes are pushed to the `main` branch. You can adjust

